    "body": "`PipelineEngine.eval_batch` fails when `loss_fn` returns more than one loss, e.g. `(loss, aux)`, which the forward pass already stores per micro-batch.\n\nTwo places broke:\n- `_reduce_outputs` looped `for idx, out in outputs`, using the first loss as a list index (`TypeError`).\n- With the default `bcast_loss=True`, `_bcast_pipe_scalar` only handles one tensor. On 2 stages the loss stage raised and the other stage hung in the broadcast.\n\nFix: sum each loss over the micro-batches by position. For the broadcast, the loss stage sends the number of losses, then all of them stacked into one tensor, as `_aggregate_total_loss` does for additional losses. A single loss takes the old path.\n\nTests:\n- New `TestPipeEvalTupleLoss` (2 stages, `bcast_loss` True and False) passes; on master it hangs.\n- New `test_pipe_reduce_outputs.py` fails on master, passes here.\n- `TestPipeGradientAccumulationScaling` still passes; 1-stage gloo run returns the per-loss means. yapf and flake8 clean.\n",
    "changed_files": 3,
    "closed_at": null,
